# 5. BUSINESS RULES — SOURCE OF TRUTH

Implement the following rules exactly.

## 5.1 REJECT RULES

A supplier pack must be REJECTED if any one of the following applies.

R01 — Excessive unit price

The quoted unit price is more than 3% above the maximum unit price in the purchase request.

Formula:

price_deviation = ((quoted_price - maximum_price) / maximum_price) * 100

If price_deviation > 3%, REJECT.

R02 — Excessive advance payment

If advance payment is greater than 20%, REJECT.

R03 — Missing late-delivery penalty clause

If the contract contains no late-delivery penalty clause, REJECT.

R04 — Missing TIN

If supplier TIN is missing, REJECT.

R05 — Missing BIN

If supplier BIN is missing, REJECT.

R06 — Excessive delivery period

If delivery is promised more than 45 days after the purchase order date, REJECT.

R07 — Insufficient late-delivery penalty rate

The contract must provide a penalty of at least 0.5% of order value per week of delay.

Implement a separate validation for this additional requirement.

A penalty below the required minimum must be treated as REJECT, subject to documenting this explicit interpretation.

A penalty clause whose rate, calculation basis, or time period is ambiguous must trigger human review unless a separate rejection condition is established.

## 5.2 NEEDS A PERSON TO CHECK RULES

If no rejection condition applies, the supplier pack must be sent for human review if any one of these conditions applies.

H01 — Minor price deviation

The quoted unit price is above the maximum price but no more than 3% above it.

H02 — Quantity deviation

The quoted quantity differs from the requested quantity by more than 5%.

Formula:

quantity_deviation = abs(quoted_quantity - requested_quantity) / requested_quantity * 100

If quantity_deviation > 5%, human review.

H03 — Payment terms

Payment terms are unclear or outside 30 to 60 days after delivery.

The remaining payment deadline must be clearly stated and measured from delivery.

H04 — Delivery period

Delivery is promised in 31 to 45 days after the purchase order date.

H05 — VAT

VAT is not separately shown at 15%.

H06 — Arithmetic inconsistency

Line totals, subtotal, VAT, or grand total do not add up.

H07 — Quotation validity

Quotation validity is less than 30 days.

H08 — Uncertainty and missing evidence

If a critical field cannot be reliably extracted, verified, or matched to its source evidence, request human review.

H09 — Conflicting information

If quotation and contract documents contradict each other regarding price, quantity, delivery, payment, supplier identity, or another material term, request human review unless an explicit rejection condition is independently established.

H10 — Ambiguous document association

If a quotation and contract cannot be reliably associated with the same supplier and purchase request, request human review.

## 5.3 APPROVE RULE

APPROVE only when:

- All mandatory information is available.
- All relevant extracted values have supporting evidence.
- All requested items are correctly matched.
- All price comparisons pass.
- All quantity comparisons pass.
- All payment terms comply.
- All delivery conditions comply.
- VAT is separately shown at 15%.
- TIN and BIN are present.
- A compliant late-delivery penalty clause exists.
- All financial calculations are correct.
- Quotation validity is at least 30 days.
- No rejection rule is triggered.
- No human-review rule or unresolved uncertainty exists.

Decision priority:

REJECT > NEEDS A PERSON TO CHECK > APPROVE.

Evaluate all rules and preserve all findings even when an earlier rejection condition has already been identified.

